series, not a certificate that travels. Slice 55 validated this
construction on BTC over 85 full-sample trades (z +0.632, KS p
0.5386, 0% incomplete). The OOS window has 41. Halving the trade
count widens the rotation null and changes the incomplete rate, so
it is measured here rather than cited from there.

PREDICTED BEFORE THIS RUN (EDGE.md 39d, committed before the
module existed): the smaller sample makes the carry offset HARDER
to detect, so |z| should come in at or below slice 55's 0.632 and
the risk to this control is clause (c) INCOMPLETES, not bias. If
it fails clause (a) upward instead, the prediction was wrong and
that goes to a human, not into a patch in this file.

Rotations are confined to the OOS window. Letting replicates land
on early dates the real rule was forbidden to trade would not be a
null for this measurement — it would compare two strategies.

